after #261 2026-09-09 — #261 M5: the behaviour gate stops grading its own ledger — the write is opt-in

knowledge/_BEHAVIOUR-GATE.md is TRACKED and was rewritten by the gate that grades it,
so a drift in the measured bytes was ABSORBED into the tracked file instead of going
red. Second instance of the class (the _screen-gate clobber repaired at M3 is the
first), which is what makes it a class rather than a wart.

The repo's own --check convention: --write refreshes the ledger; the DEFAULT run
compares and REDS, naming the remedy. The report carries no timestamp, so it is a
pure function of the sources. _build_all.py's no-argument call is now the CHECKING
form, which is what a build gate should be.

Receipts:
  two default runs — md5 ab4fbdb2 -> ab4fbdb2 -> ab4fbdb2, NO DIFF (no write at all)
  two --write runs — ab4fbdb2 -> ab4fbdb2, NO DIFF (idempotent)
  drift probe: one appended line -> default run exits 1 with LEDGER DRIFT and the
  ledger md5 is UNCHANGED after the red (65b0e367), i.e. not absorbed; --write
  restores it byte-identical to the pre-probe file
  --selftest green

The ledger body committed here is the refresh owed by M4's donut numbers.
